					<key>comment</key>
					<string>The lexer scans a whole alphanumeric word starting with a digit as one literal, so these do too: a malformed spelling reads as one bad number rather than as a number stuck to an identifier. A radix point needs an alphanumeric after it, and an exponent sign needs a lowercase `e` or `p` before it. A literal written directly after `.` or `-&gt;` never forms a real, which is what makes `t.0.Op()` a member access.</string>
