						</dict>
					</dict>
					<key>comment</key>
					<string>Every name written here is a type: that is what the context means, whatever the name's spelling. An argument reads the same way as the name it is applied to, which is how `Optional(Slice(i32))` comes out; a qualifier is taken by the rule above. A leading `.` designates a member of a struct type or of an interface, so a qualifier has to precede the dot.</string>
